      "id": "new-jersey-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://pub.njleg.gov/statutes/STATUTES-TEXT.zip",
      "title": "The legal holidays of New Jersey (N.J.S.A. 36:1-1(a), (c)) that\n`us-federal-holidays` does not already close: Good Friday, Juneteenth\nDay on the third Friday in June (the federal day is June 19) and the\ngeneral election day, held in New Jersey every year on the Tuesday after\nthe first Monday in November (N.J.S.A. 19:2-3, not vendored). FRCP\n6(a)(6)(C) and FRBP 9006(a)(6)(C) make them legal holidays of the\nDistrict of New Jersey for a period counted forward only (core's\n`frcp6-new-jersey` and `frbp9006-new-jersey`). The other § 36:1-1(a) days\nare federal holidays too, observed on the same days (36:1-1(b) moves a\nSunday holiday to Monday, 36:1-1.2 a Saturday one to the Friday before);\nSaturdays (36:1-1.1) are closed by `weekend`.\n\nEach day is closed from the date the vendored text is dated (the\nLegislature's bulk file of October 29, 2026) to the end of 2050. Not\nmodeled: Lincoln's Birthday (February 12), which 36:1-1(d) takes out of\nState government business, so the courts of the State are open on it (a\nlast day on it stays the earlier date); and the days of fasting, prayer\nor bank holidays the Governor or the President appoints, which no\nvendored source lists."
    }
